language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session3_exodus: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Five children at Hebrew school (Bernice, Carl, Debby, Sammy and Ted) each told a different part of the Exodus story (burning bush, captivity, Moses's youth, Passover, Ten Commandments). Each child is a different age (three, five, seven, eight or ten), and each family came to America from a different country (Ethiopia, Kazakhstan, Lithuania, Morocco or Yemen). Find the age, country and story of each child. Clues: (1) Debby's family is from Lithuania. (2) The child who told the Passover story is two years older than Bernice. (3) The child whose family is from Yemen is younger than the child from the Ethiopian family. (4) The child from the Moroccan family is three years older than Ted. (5) Sammy is three years older than the child who told the story of Moses's youth.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session3_exodus.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ n: the number of children, families and stories
letting n = 5
$ AV[v]: the age in years of age slot v, in the order three, five, seven, eight, ten
letting AV = [3, 5, 7, 8, 10]

$ ages[v]: the bundle number (1 to n) of the age in slot v; the same number links an age, a child, a country and a story
find ages : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
$ children[c]: the bundle number of child c, in the order Bernice, Carl, Debby, Sammy, Ted
find children : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
$ countries[k]: the bundle number of country k, in the order Ethiopia, Kazakhstan, Lithuania, Morocco, Yemen
find countries : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
$ stories[s]: the bundle number of story s, in the order burning bush, captivity, Moses's youth, Passover, Ten Commandments
find stories : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

$ search hint: branch on the child and country assignments first (speeds up the search)
branching on [children, countries, stories, ages]

such that
$ every age slot, child, country and story gets a different bundle number
allDiff(ages),
allDiff(children),
allDiff(countries),
allDiff(stories),
$ clue 1: Debby's family is from Lithuania, so child 3 and country 3 share a bundle
children[3] = countries[3],
$ clue 2: the child who told the Passover story is two years older than Bernice (child 1)
forAll a, c : int(1..n) . ((ages[a] = stories[4] /\ ages[c] = children[1]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 2),
$ clue 3: the child whose family is from Yemen (country 5) is younger than the child from the Ethiopian family (country 1)
forAll a, c : int(1..n) . ((ages[a] = countries[5] /\ ages[c] = countries[1]) -> AV[a] < AV[c]),
$ clue 4: the child from the Moroccan family (country 4) is three years older than Ted (child 5)
forAll a, c : int(1..n) . ((ages[a] = countries[4] /\ ages[c] = children[5]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 3),
$ clue 5: Sammy (child 4) is three years older than the child who told the story of Moses's youth (story 3)
forAll a, c : int(1..n) . ((ages[a] = children[4] /\ ages[c] = stories[3]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 3)
